# Impeccable Harden Rules

Harden means making UI robust, resilient, and reliable.

---

## Core Principle

Assume things will fail.

UI must continue to work even when data, images, or interactions fail.

---

## Handle All States

Always handle:

- loading
- success
- empty
- error

Never leave blank or broken UI.

---

## Defensive UI

- Avoid crashes
- Avoid layout breaking
- Validate data before rendering

---

## Edge Cases

Handle:

- long text
- missing data
- large data sets
- unexpected values

---

## Fallbacks

- Images must have fallback
- Data must have default values
- UI must degrade gracefully

---

## Reliability Over Fancy

- Prefer stable UI over complex effects
- Do not sacrifice usability for visuals

---

## Testing Mindset

- Test:
  - slow network
  - empty data
  - mobile view
  - extreme content
- Fix all breakpoints

---

## Constraints

- Do not change business logic
- Maintain readability
- Keep UI simple and stable

---

## Goal

The UI should feel:

- reliable
- stable
- resilient
- trustworthy
